Open Databricks workspace and sync latest repo code so both notebooks are current: nb_fsr_chunking_index_eval.py and nb_fsr_eval_harness.py.

Start Layer 1 first by opening nb_fsr_chunking_index_eval.py.

Run the first install cell (%pip) in that notebook and wait for success.

Run the Python restart cell (dbutils.library.restartPython), then re-run imports/widgets cells after restart.

Set Layer 1 baseline widgets:
BASELINE_METADATA_TABLE, BASELINE_CHUNK_TABLE, BASELINE_VS_INDEX, MLFLOW_EXPERIMENT, RUN_NAME_PREFIX, EMBEDDING_DIMENSION, FSR_VS_ENDPOINT, CANDIDATE_ID.

Use these Layer 1 defaults unless you are testing a different target:
- BASELINE_METADATA_TABLE = vaid.ai_sot_field_service_report.biz_metadata_field_service_report
- BASELINE_CHUNK_TABLE = vaid.ai_std_con_field_service_report.vec_field_service_report
- BASELINE_VS_INDEX = vaid.ai_std_con_field_service_report.vs_vec_field_service_report
- RUN_NAME_PREFIX = neutral label only, for example fsr_chunking_index or fsr_chunking_index_chunk500_overlap50

For baseline-only test, leave CANDIDATE_METADATA_TABLE, CANDIDATE_CHUNK_TABLE, CANDIDATE_VS_INDEX blank; for A/B test, fill candidate table/index values.

Candidate run note:
- The notebook always appends _baseline or _candidate to RUN_NAME_PREFIX.
- Do not put baseline or candidate into RUN_NAME_PREFIX itself.

Run the baseline eval cell and confirm it prints Baseline MLflow run id.

If candidate is provided, run the candidate cell and confirm Candidate MLflow run id plus JSON comparison output.

Open MLflow experiment from MLFLOW_EXPERIMENT and verify Layer 1 metrics for baseline vs candidate.

Start with these Layer 1 metrics:
- chunk_doc_coverage_ratio
- avg_chunks_per_doc
- bad_embedding_dim_count
- empty_chunk_text_count
- null_embedding_count

Move to Layer 2 by opening nb_fsr_eval_harness.py.

Run install cell (%pip), restart Python, then re-run imports/widgets cells.

Set Layer 2 widgets:
FSR_VS_ENDPOINT, FSR_VS_INDEX, FSR_METADATA_TABLE, PROBE_SET_TABLE, METADATA_VERSION (optional), PROBE_SET_VERSION, PROBE_QUERY_TEMPLATE, PROBE_PER_BUCKET, PROBE_SEED, MLFLOW_EXPERIMENT, RUN_NAME_PREFIX, TOP_K, MAX_PER_DOC, LITELLM_BASE_URL, LITELLM_API_KEY, EMBEDDING_MODEL.

Layer 2 probe-set note:
- Preferred mode for experiment 2: fill PROBE_SET_TABLE with the saved probe table.
- Leave PROBE_SET_TABLE blank only if you want the notebook to sample probes from metadata.

Run probe-set load/build cell, then run embedding smoke-test cell and confirm vector length plus healthy latency.

Run final harness cell, capture MLflow run id, then verify retrieval metrics in MLflow (avg_retrieved_vs_exists_ratio, avg_retrieved_known_fsr_count, avg_known_fsr_count, probes_succeeded, probes_failed) and compare runs by changing TOP_K/MAX_PER_DOC one knob at a time.